  {
   "title": "Some Aspects of the Antarctic Whaling Industry of Japan",
   "doc_type": "consular report with appendix",
   "start_page": 1,
   "end_page": 20,
   "continues_previous": false,
   "date": "1938-12-02",
   "from": "Beppo R. Johansen, American Vice Consul, Yokohama",
   "to": "Department of State",
   "about": "Reviews the growth, regulation, fleet, current season and trade association of Japan’s Antarctic whaling industry.",
   "summary": "The report traces Japan’s rapid increase in Antarctic whale-oil production from 1934 to 1938 and compares its fleet and output with other countries. It summarizes government controls, lists factory ships and proposed expansion, and describes the 1938–39 season’s personnel, supply routes and intended use of whale meat and hides. It also summarizes the Japan Whaling Association’s rules and identifies published and confidential sources. Page 20 reproduces Japanese regulatory text cited in the report.",
   "keywords": [
    "Antarctic whaling",
    "factory ships",
    "whale oil",
    "whaling ordinance",
    "Japan Whaling Association"
   ]
  },
  {
