  {
   "title": "The Training of Personnel for Japanese Fisheries",
   "doc_type": "consular report",
   "start_page": 25,
   "end_page": 61,
   "continues_previous": false,
   "date": "1940-03-16",
   "from": "W. Garland Richardson, American Vice Consul, Tokyo",
   "to": "Department of State",
   "about": "Surveys Japanese fisheries schools, higher instruction, training vessels and research stations.",
   "summary": "Richardson describes preparatory and prefectural schools, the Hakodate Higher Fisheries School, the Fisheries Institute and Tokyo Imperial University’s fisheries course. He details admission rules, curricula, staff, students, graduates, foreign enrolment, vessels and training stations. The report also explains the organization and services of prefectural and central fisheries experimental stations. It ends with a list of sources; its separately titled translated regulations follow.",
   "keywords": [
